The grammar of interpreted code, production by production.

Each heading is a production of SuperCollider's own grammar (the Bison file
lang/LangSource/Bison/lang11d of version 3.14.1), written as that file
writes it, or `lexer ...` for something its lexer does (PyrLexer.cpp).
Headings that follow one another share the forms under them. The forms, one
to a paragraph, are the shortest code that reaches the production, and then
whatever else of its kind seemed worth asking. Where no code can reach a
production, a line that begins `-- ` says why. tests/lang11d.rs requires of
every form that sclang compiles it, that our grammar parses it without an
error, and that sclang compiles the formatted form to the same thing; and,
when SuperCollider's source is there to read, that every production of
lang11d is a heading here or in classes.forms. The forms are ours; nothing
here is copied from SuperCollider.

